================================================================================
CHALLENGE 2: THE HOT-SWAP CONFIG (volatile Reference)
================================================================================
SCENARIO: Your application has a "Configuration" object. Thousands of Worker
threads read this config every second. Occasionally, an Admin thread updates
 the URL or Timeout. You need the workers to see the update INSTANTLY
without the massive performance hit of a lock.

1. CLASS: 'ServerConfig' (Immutable)
   - FIELDS: 'final String url' and 'final int timeout'.
   - Create a simple constructor to set these.

2. CLASS: 'ConfigManager' (Main)
   - VARIABLE: 'private static volatile ServerConfig config;'
   - TASK 1 (Worker): A thread that loops and prints 'config.url' every 500ms.
   - TASK 2 (Admin): A thread that sleeps for 2 seconds, then swaps the config:
     'config = new ServerConfig("https://api.v2.com", 5000);'

EXPECTATION: The Worker thread should be printing "v1" initially. The
moment the Admin thread performs the assignment, the Worker should
immediately start printing "v2" without any "stale" reads.
================================================================================